6,544).","test":"Exact binomial test of the share of women, children and people aged 60 and over against zero","statistic":{"women_children_elderly":37939,"men_18_59":34896,"n":72835},"p":0.0,"effect":{"name":"Share of dead who are women, children under 18 or aged 60+","value":0.5209,"ci":[0.517260664348258,0.5245164965600515],"population_share":0.7549},"ref":"§6.1","p_adjusted":0.0,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"52.1% of the identified dead (95% CI 51.7% to 52.5%) are women, children under 18 or people aged 60 and over, against 75.5% of the population. More than half of the dead fall outside the group from which armed men are drawn: the dead are not confined to men of fighting age."},{"id":"H2a","group":"H2","title":"The November 2023 pause and the daily killing rate","null":"The daily rate of killing during the pause of 24-30 November 2023 equalled the rate in the 14 days before it.","data":"Comparison window: Ministry of Health / Government Media Office daily series (Tech For Palestine), 10-23 November 2023. Pause: killings reported incident by incident (OCHA Flash Updates #49-#55; AP; Al Jazeera).","test":"Negative binomial regression on a pause indicator, Newey-West errors (lag 7)","statistic":{"overdispersion_alpha":1.218,"overdispersion_p":0.0},"p":2.1502422864116134e-79,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, pause against the 14 days before","value":0.0025,"ci":[0.001348295215177294,0.004677485989530692]},"descriptive":{"before_per_day":284.4,"during_per_day":0.71,"during_ci":[0.23,1.67],"during_days":7,"during_killed":5,"incidents":[{"date":"2023-11-24","killed":2,"note":"Two people shot dead returning north (AP, Al Jazeera, Gaza Ministry of Health; OCHA: at least one)"},{"date":"2023-11-26","killed":1,"note":"One man killed by tank fire east of Al-Maghazi (OCHA Flash Update #51)"},{"date":"2023-11-29","killed":2,"note":"Two people killed by Israeli fire in northern Gaza City (OCHA Flash Update #55)"}]},"sensitivity":[{"name":"Exact conditional Poisson test","value":0.0025,"ci":[0.0008149647521340257,0.005865446900026566],"p":0.0},{"name":"Against the upper bound of 40 deaths during the pause","value":0.0201,"ci":[0.014330566740483814,0.02740707521297492],"p":0.0}],"sources":[{"title":"Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel - Flash Update #49","org":"OCHA","date":"24 November 2023","url":"https://www.ochaopt.org/content/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-49"},{"title":"Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel - Flash Update #51","org":"OCHA","date":"26 November 2023","url":"https://www.ochaopt.org/content/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-51"},{"title":"Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel - Flash Update #53","org":"OCHA","date":"28 November 2023","url":"https://www.ochaopt.org/content/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-53"},{"title":"Hostilities in the Gaza Strip and Israel - Flash Update #55","org":"OCHA","date":"30 November 2023","url":"https://www.ochaopt.org/content/hostilities-gaza-strip-and-israel-flash-update-55"},{"title":"Israeli troops fire at Palestinians attempting to return to northern Gaza during cease-fire","org":"Associated Press (PBS NewsHour)","date":"24 November 2023","url":"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israeli-troops-fire-at-palestinians-attempting-to-return-to-northern-gaza-during-cease-fire"},{"title":"'The war is not over': Israel blocks Palestinians' return to northern Gaza","org":"Al Jazeera","date":"24 November 2023","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/24/displaced-people-attempt-to-return-home-across-gaza-as-truce-sets-in"}],"ref":"§13","p_adjusted":6.450726859234841e-79,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"Reported killings fell from 284.4 a day in the fortnight before the pause to 0.71 a day during it (rate ratio 0.0025, 95% CI 0.0013 to 0.0047). Killing did not stop: at least 5 people were reported killed in the 7 days. Against the upper bound of 40 deaths the ratio is 0.0201, still a fall of about 98%."},{"id":"H2b","group":"H2","title":"The January-March 2025 ceasefire and the daily killing rate","null":"The daily rate of new killings during the ceasefire (19 Jan 2025 to 17 Mar 2025) equalled the rate in the 60 days before it.","data":"Ministry of Health daily series (Tech For Palestine). Ceasefire days count new killings only where the Ministry separates them from bodies recovered.","test":"Negative binomial regression on a ceasefire indicator, Newey-West errors (lag 7)","statistic":{"overdispersion_alpha":1.651,"overdispersion_p":0.0},"p":0.0005605520405789182,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, ceasefire against the 60 days before","value":0.149,"ci":[0.050598802260787994,0.4396283938881203]},"descriptive":{"before_per_day":48.8,"during_per_day":7.28,"during_ci":[6.6,8.0],"during_days":58,"during_killed":422},"sensitivity":[{"name":"Weekly totals","value":0.152,"ci":[0.06535709085842832,0.3547302198618485],"p":1.2902502890171945e-05},{"name":"New killings only in both windows","value":0.18,"ci":[0.06518230503777639,0.49595735641381966],"p":0.0009178338548543893}],"ref":"§13","p_adjusted":0.0008408280608683773,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"New killings fell from 48.8 a day in the 60 days before to 7.28 a day during the ceasefire (rate ratio 0.149, 95% CI 0.051 to 0.44). Killing continued throughout: 422 new killings were reported in 58 days (95% CI 6.6 to 8.0 a day)."},{"id":"H2c","group":"H2","title":"The October 2025 ceasefire and the daily killing rate","null":"The daily rate of new killings during the ceasefire (10 Oct 2025 to 01 Oct 2026) equalled the rate in the 60 days before it.","data":"Ministry of Health daily series (Tech For Palestine). Ceasefire days count new killings only where the Ministry separates them from bodies recovered.","test":"Negative binomial regression on a ceasefire indicator, Newey-West errors (lag 7)","statistic":{"overdispersion_alpha":1.454,"overdispersion_p":0.0},"p":1.4475676989266635e-73,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, ceasefire against the 60 days before","value":0.039,"ci":[0.02743529696032152,0.055312256373399364]},"descriptive":{"before_per_day":96.1,"during_per_day":3.74,"during_ci":[3.54,3.95],"during_days":357,"during_killed":1336},"sensitivity":[{"name":"Weekly totals","value":0.037,"ci":[0.023386041080628302,0.057620330344167206],"p":8.453356301100016e-47},{"name":"New killings only in both windows","value":0.061,"ci":[0.046540691886794654,0.08003622082905355],"p":6.731538703881247e-91}],"ref":"§13","p_adjusted":3.6189192473166585e-73,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"New killings fell from 96.1 a day in the 60 days before to 3.74 a day during the ceasefire (rate ratio 0.039, 95% CI 0.027 to 0.055). Killing continued throughout: 1,336 new killings were reported in 357 days (95% CI 3.54 to 3.95 a day)."},{"id":"H3a","group":"H3","title":"The ICJ order of 26 January 2024 and the daily killing rate","null":"No change in the level or the slope of daily deaths at the order of 26 January 2024.","data":"Ministry of Health daily series (Tech For Palestine), 1 December 2023 to 31 July 2024.","test":"Segmented negative binomial regression (trend, and a level and slope change at each order), Newey-West errors; joint Wald test of level and slope","statistic":{"wald_chi2":0.02,"df":2,"overdispersion_alpha":0.16},"p":0.9893239884744863,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, level change at the order","value":1.006,"ci":[0.808053350101014,1.253078910811594],"slope_change_per_30_days":1.023},"ref":"§13","p_adjusted":0.9893239884744863,"result":"null not rejected","status":"run","reading":"No detectable change in the level or the trend of daily deaths at the order (level rate ratio 1.006, 95% CI 0.81 to 1.3; joint test p = 0.99). The order was not followed by a measurable fall in the rate of killing. This is the absence of a detectable change, not proof that the order had no effect on any conduct."},{"id":"H3b","group":"H3","title":"The ICJ order of 28 March 2024 and the daily killing rate","null":"No change in the level or the slope of daily deaths at the order of 28 March 2024.","data":"Ministry of Health daily series (Tech For Palestine), 1 December 2023 to 31 July 2024.","test":"Segmented negative binomial regression (trend, and a level and slope change at each order), Newey-West errors; joint Wald test of level and slope","statistic":{"wald_chi2":3.7,"df":2,"overdispersion_alpha":0.16},"p":0.15705045065644938,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, level change at the order","value":0.819,"ci":[0.6454033547306263,1.0402274233479245],"slope_change_per_30_days":1.272},"ref":"§13","p_adjusted":0.18121205844974927,"result":"null not rejected","status":"run","reading":"No detectable change in the level or the trend of daily deaths at the order (level rate ratio 0.819, 95% CI 0.65 to 1; joint test p = 0.16). The order was not followed by a measurable fall in the rate of killing. This is the absence of a detectable change, not proof that the order had no effect on any conduct."},{"id":"H3c","group":"H3","title":"The ICJ order of 24 May 2024 and the daily killing rate","null":"No change in the level or the slope of daily deaths at the order of 24 May 2024.","data":"Ministry of Health daily series (Tech For Palestine), 1 December 2023 to 31 July 2024.","test":"Segmented negative binomial regression (trend, and a level and slope change at each order), Newey-West errors; joint Wald test of level and slope","statistic":{"wald_chi2":0.42,"df":2,"overdispersion_alpha":0.16},"p":0.8122036293079367,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, level change at the order","value":1.115,"ci":[0.7026483691552746,1.7698417687613588],"slope_change_per_30_days":0.946},"ref":"§13","p_adjusted":0.8702181742585036,"result":"null not rejected","status":"run","reading":"No detectable change in the level or the trend of daily deaths at the order (level rate ratio 1.115, 95% CI 0.7 to 1.8; joint test p = 0.81). The order was not followed by a measurable fall in the rate of killing. This is the absence of a detectable change, not proof that the order had no effect on any conduct."},{"id":"H4a","group":"H4","title":"West Bank killings before and after 7 October 2023","null":"The daily rate of Palestinians killed in the West Bank was the same after 7 October 2023 as before it, within 2023.","data":"OCHA via the report: 208 killed in 279 days (1 January-6 October 2023); 299 in 86 days (7 October-31 December 2023).","test":"Exact conditional test of two Poisson rates","statistic":{"before_per_day":0.75,"after_per_day":3.48},"p":5.431133330388496e-65,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, after against before","value":4.66,"ci":[3.894070764088673,5.593472517179762]},"ref":"§11","p_adjusted":1.1638142850832491e-64,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"Palestinians were killed in the West Bank at 3.48 a day after 7 October 2023 against 0.75 before it, 4.66 times the rate (95% CI 3.89 to 5.59), in a year that was already the deadliest on record before the war began."},{"id":"H4b","group":"H4","title":"Settler incidents against Palestinians, 2024 against 2022","null":"The rate of settler incidents against Palestinians was the same in 2024 as in 2022.","data":"OCHA daily averages via the report: 2 a day in 2022, 7 a day in 2024.","test":"Exact conditional test of two Poisson rates on annual counts reconstructed from the daily averages","statistic":{"2022_per_day":2,"2024_per_day":7},"p":3.1365701239087442e-235,"effect":{"name":"Rate ratio, 2024 against 2022","value":3.5,"ci":[3.2223452895994904,3.80525686576526]},"sensitivity":[{"name":"At the rounding bounds least favourable to rejection (2.5 and 6.5 a day)","value":2.6,"ci":[2.4086231582413347,2.81034505055818],"p":5.023932564904994e-148}],"ref":"§11","p_adjusted":1.1762137964657791e-234,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"Settler incidents ran at 3.5 times the 2022 rate in 2024 (95% CI 3.22 to 3.81), and at 2.6 times even at the rounding bounds least favourable to the finding."},{"id":"H6a","group":"H6","title":"The identity numbers on the named list","null":"The identity numbers are valid Population Registry numbers (pass the check digit).","data":"Ministry of Health named list, 72,835 records.","test":"Share passing the check digit, with its interval; exact binomial test against the 10% expected of fabricated numbers; decision rule: validity rejected if under 99% pass","statistic":{"valid":72835,"n":72835},"p":0.0,"effect":{"name":"Share of identity numbers with a valid check digit","value":1.0,"ci":[0.9999472608467715,1.0]},"decision":"validity not rejected","descriptive":{"duplicate_ids":0,"duplicate_name_and_dob":0,"age_dob_checked":72835,"age_dob_disagree":0},"ref":"§6.1","p_adjusted":0.0,"result":"validity not rejected; the 10% fabrication benchmark is rejected","status":"run","reading":"All 72,835 of the 72,835 identity numbers pass the Population Registry check digit, where fabricated numbers would pass about one time in ten. There are 0 duplicate identity numbers and 0 duplicate name-and-birth-date pairs, and the stated age agrees with the date of birth in 72,835 of 72,835 records. The list as published is consistent with registry data. These tests cannot detect a real identity number attached to someone who did not die; that question needs matching against other records."},{"id":"H6b","group":"H6","title":"Age heaping on the named list","null":"Age reporting shows no more heaping on ages ending in 0 and 5 than a registry-based list would.","data":"As H6a.","test":"Whipple's index (ages 23-62) on the UN scale, and Myers' blended index (ages 10-89), against the PCBS 2017 census","statistic":{"whipple":100.0,"myers":0.85},"p":null,"effect":{"name":"Whipple's index","value":100.0,"scale":"highly accurate","census_whipple":100.0,"census_myers":2.4},"digits":[10.22,9.91,10.0,9.85,9.83,9.67,9.89,10.05,10.0,10.57],"ages":[1072,1052,1113,1045,1011,1116,1077,1140,1064,1088,1085,1150,1218,1329,1453,1425,1591,1608,1648,1708,1628,1589,1612,1555,1489,1516,1543,1576,1678,1818,1743,1673,1737,1598,1561,1462,1325,1271,1103,1106,934,921,810,828,759,698,648,654,600,572,585,509,471,477,466,428,475,437,401,412,438,382,351,314,291,294,268,264,237,231,234,177,192,181,185,144,137,118,91,66,66,83,78,49,44,31,46,38,25,25,14,27,15,9,3,3,8,9,1,0,1],"ref":"§6.1","status":"run","result":"highly accurate","reading":"No age heaping: Whipple's index is 100.0 and Myers' index 0.85, against the 2017 census's 100 and 2.4. Ages on the list follow from registry dates of birth rather than estimates, which is what a list built from identity records, and not from guesses, should show."},{"id":"H8b","group":"H8","title":"Recognition of Palestine and calling it genocide","null":"Whether a UN member state government has called it genocide is independent of whether it recognises Palestine.","data":"World positions dataset, 193 UN member states.","test":"Fisher's exact test (interval with Haldane correction for a zero cell)","statistic":{"recognises_and_yes":50,"recognises_and_no":107,"does_not_and_yes":0,"does_not_and_no":36},"p":9.233605653279527e-06,"effect":{"name":"Odds ratio","value":34.29,"ci":[2.0631915898927997,569.9962377633104]},"ref":"§15.4","p_adjusted":1.538934275546588e-05,"result":"null rejected","status":"run","reading":"50 of 157 recognising states have a government that has called it genocide; none of the 36 non-recognising states has (odds ratio 34.29, with a correction for the empty cell)."}]}